# SandBase over plain HTTP. Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Set your key below (or in an http-client env file) and click "Send Request" above each block.

@base = https://api.sandbase.ai
@key = sk-YOUR_KEY

### Sync data API: the result comes back in this response
POST {{base}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "model": "exa/search", "query": "AI agents", "numResults": 3 }

### Same call, path form (data APIs only): body without "model"
POST {{base}}/v1/api/exa/search
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "AI agents", "numResults": 3 }

### Async capability: returns {"id", "status": "pending"}
# @name submit
POST {{base}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "model": "app-store/search", "term": "notes" }

### Poll until status is completed or failed
GET {{base}}/v1/run/{{submit.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}

### What the run cost
GET {{base}}/v1/tasks/{{submit.response.body.id}}/cost
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}

### Image (sync): price depends on quality and resolution, see catalog/models/openai/gpt-image-2.5-flare.json
POST {{base}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "model": "openai/gpt-image-2.5-flare", "prompt": "a red apple on a white table", "quality": "low", "resolution": "1k" }

### Video (async) with a callback instead of polling
POST {{base}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "model": "bytedance/seedance/2.5/text-to-video", "prompt": "a cat surfing at sunset", "duration": 4, "resolution": "480p",
  "webhook_url": "https://example.com/sandbase-callback" }

### LLM, OpenAI-compatible
POST {{base}}/v1/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "model": "openai/gpt-6.1-sol", "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Hello" }] }

### Account balance
GET {{base}}/v1/account/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}

### Agents: create an Agent
# @name agent
POST {{base}}/v1/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-example-agent-1

{ "name": "HTTP example", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "instructions": "Answer in one short sentence." }

### Run it: create a Session with the first input
# @name session
POST {{base}}/v1/agents/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-example-session-1

{ "agent_id": "{{agent.response.body.id}}", "input": "What is 2+2?" }

### Turns (newest first): wait until the first one is "completed"
GET {{base}}/v1/agents/sessions/{{session.response.body.id}}/turns
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}

### Read the answer
GET {{base}}/v1/agents/sessions/{{session.response.body.id}}/items?order=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}

### Sandbox templates (E2B control API; use the E2B SDK for commands and files)
GET https://sandbox.sandbase.ai/v2/templates?limit=100
X-API-Key: {{key}}
